  "abstract_en": {
   "value": "Um, Ik-Cheon* · Hwang, Won-Sik**\nThe aim of this study is to analyze effects of portfolio changes in public R&D investments on the Korean economy. To that end, we developed a computable general equilibrium model that enables industry-specific simulations. This study is distinguished from others in that it focused on public R&D investments of two major sectors in Korea: steel and semiconductor industries. The simulation results show that an increase of public R&D investment in the steel industry has a positive effect on the whole economy. On the other hand, an increase of public R&D investment in the semiconductor industry has a positive effect to some extent, but gives a negative effect on the national economy. This implies that there is an optimal point of public R&D investment in each industry.",
